-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (deposited text: ../../registers/source-bundle/TA1999.txt)
-- and the instruments made under it -- NOUNS ONLY.
-- This module holds DECLARE and nothing else: the things a witness of ordinary competence could testify to
-- (what a piece of equipment does and by what means, where it is, what the person holds, a fine, a term of
-- imprisonment).  Every other sgta- module imports it.  It has no rules and no directives.
--
-- What the Act's own words are is not a noun.  Whether a thing "is radio-communication equipment" is worked out
-- in sgta-s2-definitions.l4 from the facts below; whether a person "commits an offence" is worked out in
-- sgta-part6-offences.l4.

-- The three acts of "telecommunications" (s 2): "a transmission, emission or reception of signs, signals, writing,
-- images, sounds or intelligence of any nature".
DECLARE `Telecommunication act` IS ONE OF
    `transmission`
    `emission`
    `reception`

-- The means in the definition of "telecommunications" (s 2): "by wire, radio, optical or other electromagnetic
-- systems".  "Radio" is the means "Hertzian or radio waves" in the definition of "radio-communication".
DECLARE `Means of telecommunication` IS ONE OF
    `wire`
    `Hertzian or radio waves`
    `optical or other electromagnetic system`

-- A piece of equipment as a witness could describe it: what it is called, what it is used or intended to be used
-- to do, and by what means.  A satellite-navigation receiver has the act `reception` and the means
-- `Hertzian or radio waves`; a walkie-talkie has `transmission` and `reception` by the same means.
DECLARE `A piece of equipment` HAS
    `what it is called` IS A STRING
    `acts it is used or intended to be used for` IS A LIST OF `Telecommunication act`
    `means it uses` IS A LIST OF `Means of telecommunication`

-- The acts the Act speaks of in relation to a telecommunication system or service: the privilege of s 3(2)(a)
-- ("establishing, installing, using, working, maintaining, developing, constructing, promoting, hiring and selling"),
-- s 3(1) ("operation and provision") and the offence of s 53(1) ("establishes, installs, maintains, provides or operates").
DECLARE `Act on a telecommunication system or service` IS ONE OF
    `establishing`
    `installing`
    `using`
    `working`
    `maintaining`
    `developing`
    `constructing`
    `promoting`
    `hiring`
    `selling`
    `providing`
    `operating`

-- Where equipment is (s 55(1): "in any place or on board any vessel, aircraft or in any vehicle in Singapore").
DECLARE `Where the equipment is` IS ONE OF
    `in a place in Singapore`
    `on board a vessel`
    `on board an aircraft`
    `in a vehicle in Singapore`

-- The kinds of craft the definition of "vessel" (s 2) names, so that "vessel" can be worked out.
DECLARE `Kind of craft` IS ONE OF
    `a ship`
    `a boat`
    `an air-cushioned vehicle`
    `a floating rig or platform used in any form of operations at sea`
    `any other description of vessel`
    `not a vessel`

-- What a person holds, as that person could state it.  The fields are the routes the Act itself names:
-- s 54(1) ("a licence granted under section 5 or any regulations made under this Act"), s 56 (a licence issued in
-- a treaty country and recognised here), s 96 (exemption by the Minister) and s 95 (licensing under the
-- Broadcasting Act 1994, which is not this Act's business).
DECLARE `What the person holds` HAS
    `a licence granted under section 5` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an authorisation given by regulations made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an exemption given by the Minister under section 96` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a licence issued in a treaty country and recognised under section 56` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- placeholder: no sgta- rule reads this field; s 95 is applied through its own inputs (see NOTES.md)
    `a licence under the Broadcasting Act 1994 for this apparatus` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What a section says a person may be made to suffer at most on conviction.
-- Where an Act says "a fine not exceeding $X or imprisonment not exceeding Y or both", each figure is a ceiling
-- and the court may impose either or both: the record holds the two ceilings, not a sentence.
DECLARE `Penalty` HAS
    `fine not exceeding` IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment not exceeding, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `further daily fine after conviction, not exceeding` IS A NUMBER
    `articles seized are forfeited in addition` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The result of asking whether a provision makes something an offence, and what it costs.
DECLARE `Offence outcome` IS ONE OF
    `an offence under` HAS `provision` IS A STRING
                           `penalty` IS A `Penalty`
    `no offence under this provision`

-- The equipment that the exemption notification "Telecommunications (Exemption from sections 33, 34(1)(b) and 35)
-- Notification" (N 1) names in its Schedule(s), by the title the Schedule gives it, across all its vintages.
-- (Frequency bands and power limits are not modelled; see sgta-i-n1-exemption.l4.)
DECLARE `N 1 schedule item` IS ONE OF
    `CB Walkie Talkie Transceivers`
    `Multi-channel Walkie Talkie Transceivers`
    `Wireless Microphones`
    `CB Band Radio Paging Systems`
    `Induction Loop Communication Systems`
    `VHF Radio Paging System`
    `Radio Detection and Alarm Systems`
    `Medical and Biological Telemetry Devices`
    `Wireless Modem`
    `Radio Telemetry Equipment`
    `Remote Control Devices (a) Garage Door Openers`
    `Remote Control Devices (b) Cameras`
    `Remote Control Devices (c) Toys and Robots`
    `Remote Control Devices (d) Battery-operated Cars and Boats`
    `Remote Control Devices (e) TV Receivers or Radio Systems`
    `Remote Control Devices (f) Other Miscellaneous Remote Control Devices`
    `Cordless Telephones or Wireless PABX`
    `Wireless LAN or Low Power Devices`
    `Wireless LAN, RFID or Low Power Devices`
    `Stand-alone GPS Receivers`
    `Global Navigation Satellite Systems Receivers`
    `Communication Receivers (excluding Scanning devices) and MMDS Receivers`
    `Short Range Radar System`
    `Hearing Aids and Audio Assistance Aids`
    `Ultra-Wideband Devices`
    `Intelligent Transport System`
    `Fixed White Space Devices`
    `Portable Mode I White Space Devices`
    `Portable Mode II White Space Devices`

-- The public systems of Rg 5 reg 65(4) to which a station must be connected (or capable of being connected) for the
-- class licence of reg 65.
DECLARE `Public system of Rg 5 reg 65(4)` IS ONE OF
    `a public cellular mobile telephone system`
    `a public radio paging system`
    `a public mobile data system`
    `a public trunked radio system`
    `a public satellite mobile telephone or data system`
    `a public wireless broadband access system`

-- What the consolidation's own margin markers say about when a section's wording last changed.
-- ("no marker" is a fact about the deposit, not a statement that the wording never changed.)
DECLARE `Marker history` IS ONE OF
    `no amendment marker after the 2000 Revised Edition`
    `last marked amendment began on` HAS `day` IS A NUMBER
                                         `month` IS A NUMBER
                                         `year` IS A NUMBER


-- A fee that the Radio-communication Regulations state for a period rather than per annum ("$100 for 5 years").
DECLARE `A fee for a period` HAS
    `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `for how many years` IS A NUMBER
